  "summary": "Santa Rosa Police Chief John Cregan held a community forum drawing 400-500 people to discuss the department's 143 Flock ALPR cameras, facing largely critical residents concerned about data sharing with outside agencies and vendor contract changes. Cregan said the department has already adjusted procedures based on feedback and pledged ongoing engagement.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Flock isn't responsible. Flock lies. They've changed their contract to where they have an irrevocable license, in perpetuity, to our data",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    },
    {
      "quote": "Santa Rosa police access the data approximately 5,000 times a month, outside agencies look at Santa Rosa Flock data 486,000 times a month",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    },
    {
      "quote": "Are there ways that we can tighten up our policies, tighten our protocols and make sure that at the end of the day we have the trust of our community",
      "paragraph_idx": 11
    }
  ],
